.env
# `data/raw/*` (not a bare directory pattern) so the negations below can
# un-ignore individual files - git can't un-ignore a file whose parent
# directory is itself excluded from traversal.
data/raw/*
# Completed-season football-data.co.uk CSVs are immutable once the season ends,
# so they are committed - like understat_xg.csv below - and an unattended CI run
# never depends on that host being up to fetch them. Only the in-progress
# season (config.CURRENT_SEASON) is re-pulled each run and left untracked; add
# the next `!data/raw/*_<season>.csv` line when CURRENT_SEASON rolls over.
!data/raw/*_2324.csv
!data/raw/*_2425.csv
!data/raw/*_2526.csv
# `data/processed/*` (not a bare directory pattern) so the negation below
# can actually un-ignore one file inside it - git can't un-ignore a file
# whose parent directory itself is excluded from traversal.
data/processed/*
# xG changes slowly (only as matches are played) and Understat has no
# official API - cache it in the repo rather than re-pull it every CI run,
# per the project's own "cache Understat aggressively" rule. Refresh
# manually with `python -m ingest.understat` every so often, not on schedule.
!data/processed/understat_xg.csv
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# `artefacts/*` (not a bare directory pattern) so the negation below can
# actually un-ignore one file inside it - same reasoning as data/processed/*
# above. prediction_log.csv is the standing, append-only record a public
# track record is scored from (evaluate.prediction_log) - it belongs in git
# history like any other record, not regenerated on every run.
artefacts/*
!artefacts/prediction_log.csv
.pytest_cache/
